            "review_title": "Review at Đặc Sản Hoàng Tín",
            "review_text": "1Hermes1\nAbu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates23 contributions\n0\nFun local place\nJun 2016 • Couples\nThis is a small place where you can make your own rolls (not fried but the kind where you roll veggies and meat in rice paper). \nThe veggies are super-fresh and the place was one of the cleanest I've been to in Vietnam. They've got a hand washing station at the back which is very clean. \nService was excellent with the staff very happy to see foreigners (I don't think many visit). Our guide from Hue took us here and told us this is a popular family restaurant for locals. \nWe had (spring?) rolls with two types of pork and pork noodle soup (thick rice noodles - similar to udon). Great place for a quick lunch without (other) tourists. \nNote: There's a pet shop (the usual sad sight of puppies in very small cages, etc.) two doors down the street which western tourists may want to avoid before eating.\nRead more\nWritten June 6, 2016",
